The right engine sustained damage from ingesting a taxiway light, and the thrust reverser and inlet cowls were damaged. Two fan blades of the left engine were bent.  The left and right inboard aft flaps were damaged. The damage did not meet the 49 CFR Part 830 definition of “substantial.”&#x0D;
