&#x0D;
2 Navigation tracks are over ocean routes that are assigned to flights to separate them from other overwater aircraft in a non-radar environment.  Aircraft report to oceanic air traffic control facilities at fixed reporting points, thus notifying these facilities of their flight progress.&#x0D;
